  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=\u27e8\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{2}-3,\\,1-t\u27e9$ at $t=1?$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=1$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =\u27e8\\sqrt{1+1},{1}^{2}-3,1-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\sqrt{2},1-3,1-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\sqrt{2},-2,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=1$ is the vector $\u27e8\\sqrt{2},-2,0\u27e9.$",
